      "text": "The Filipinos Do Not Yield (FDNY) Movement, along with various groups, hold a lightning protest in front of the Chinese Embassy along Sen. Gil Puyat Avenue in Makati City on Monday, May 11.\n\nThe protesters condemned the continued harassment, intimidation, and aggressive presence of Chinese ships in the West Philippine Sea, as well as China’s statement that the Philippines is “playing with fire” because of its alliances and preparations for self-defense. Protesters also held placards and burned a cardboard replica of a Chinese Coast Guard ship to express their anger. \n\n📸: Mark Balmores/MB",
